<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Shoredits put under judicial management.</title>
<headline>Shoredits put under judicial management.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shoredits Holdings Ltd said on Monday that the company had been put under provisional judicial management with effect from January 24.</p>
<p>The building and construction group had announced last week that it was seeking to recapitalise after Samrand Development Holdings Ltd terminated talks which would have led to Samrand acquiring a controlling interest in Shoredits.  </p>
<p>Shareholders were urged to exercise caution in their dealings. Shoredits gave no further details in a brief announcement.</p>
<p>The company's shares have fallen sharply from a high of 380 cents in January 1996. They closed on Friday at 55 cents after reaching a low of 25 cents on January 22.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
